// PURPOSE:
// Formal specification of DVSM energy-aware execution model.
// This section is NON-executable and serves as system theory.
//
// =====================================================
// MARK: - SYSTEM ENERGY INVARIANT
// =====================================================
//
// DVSM sustainability MUST preserve:
//
//   1. Determinism
//   2. Auditability
//   3. Identifiability invariants
//
// under all resource constraints.
//
// Constraint:
//
//   ∀ execution state S, ∃ budget R such that:
//       F(S) is deterministic regardless of R
//
// =====================================================
// MARK: - RESOURCE-AWARE EXECUTION RULE
// =====================================================
//
// Let:
//
//   C = compute budget
//   G = governance depth
//   A = audit completeness
//
// Execution rule:
//
//   if C < threshold:
//       reduce G
//       batch A
//       delay non-critical operations
//
// BUT:
//   critical invariants MUST always execute.
//
// =====================================================
// MARK: - RACE-TO-SLEEP MODEL
// =====================================================
//
// DVSM supports deferred execution windows:
//
//   - batch governance checks
//   - coalesce audit writes
//   - reduce wake cycles
//
// Objective:
//
//   minimize energy consumption while preserving correctness.
//
// =====================================================
// MARK: - SAFETY GUARANTEE
// =====================================================
//
// No sustainability mode is allowed to:
//
//   - break determinism
//   - remove audit traceability
//   - disable critical governance validation
//
// ultraLowPower mode is:
//
//   a bounded reduction of execution scope,
//   NOT a removal of correctness constraints.
//
// =====================================================
// MARK: - FORMAL INTERPRETATION
// =====================================================
//
// DVSM optimization objective:
//
//   minimize(energy)
//
// subject to:
//
//   correctness ∧ auditability ∧ identifiability
//
// =====================================================
// Key:
// public static let originator = DVSMAuthor(
    fullName: "Daniel J. Dillberg",
    identifier: "dj-dillberg",
    role: "DVSM v16.x System Architect"
)
//
// =====================================================
//
// CORE PRINCIPLE:
//
// DVSM is a constrained optimization system:
//
//   preserve correctness
//   minimize energy usage
//   maintain deterministic auditability
//
